    "result_text": "The full suite (the single `AcceptanceTest` class, plus its support files) passes with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `sharesHousehold` / `householdId` feature by extending the existing household logic rather than duplicating it.\n\n**Behavior:** When a create-owner request sets `sharesHousehold: true` and an existing owner already occupies the same household (same last name + address, compared case-insensitively with collapsed whitespace), the new owner and every existing member are given one shared, stable `householdId`, which is returned on `GET /api/owners/{id}`. An id already held by a member is reused; otherwise a stable one is derived from the household key and back-filled onto existing members. The pre-existing 409 rejection for un-opted-in duplicates is unchanged.\n\n**Changes:**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added read-only `householdId` to the `Owner` schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` and the MapStruct mapping pick it up automatically).\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 added the `household_id` column and accessors.\n- `db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql` \u2014 added the `household_id` column.\n- `function/owner/Household.java` \u2014 **new** small helper holding the shared household identity logic: `canonical(...)`, `matches(...)`, and `idFor(...)`. This is the single home for what was previously private canonicalization inside `EnsureUniqueHousehold`.\n- `function/owner/EnsureUniqueHousehold.java` \u2014 refactored to reuse `Household.matches(...)` instead of its own copy.\n- `function/owner/AssignHousehold.java` \u2014 **new** pipeline step, single responsibility: assign the shared id when opting in.\n- `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` \u2014 wired `assignHousehold` after `build`, under `transaction` governance so the back-fill of existing members commits with the create.\n\nEach step keeps one public method and one job; `EnsureUniqueHousehold` still owns rejection, `AssignHousehold` owns id assignment, and both share `Household` for the matching rule.",
